<title>JAPAN: Finnish Export Credit launches dual samurai - Nikko.</title>
<headline>Finnish Export Credit launches dual samurai - Nikko.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following dual-currency samurai issue was announced by lead-manager Nikko Securities on Thursday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Finnish Export Credit</p>
<p> AMT		 30 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    3.00 pct</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> MATURITY	  1 February, 2001</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  1 August, 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	July 24 to July 31</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AA, Moody's Aa1</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Nikko Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Nikko Trust and Banking</p>
<p>NOTES: The exchange rate was fixed at $4,630.49 per 500,000 yen.</p>
<p>---Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-9780</p>
</text>
